Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [M156] [optimization_guide] Defer SetInput() callbacks to
 avoid UAF

Original change's description:
> [optimization_guide] Defer SetInput() callbacks to avoid UAF
>
> AIManager binds ownership of a pending OnDeviceSession into its
> SetInput() callback, causing a use-after-free if SessionImpl or
> OnDeviceContext runs or drops that callback with `this` still on the
> stack, and hanging/leaking if GetOrCreateSession() has an empty input
> context or the service disconnects mid-prefill.
>
> Wrap non-null callbacks with base::BindPostTaskToCurrentDefault() in
> SessionImpl::AddContextImpl() (adding one task hop rather than brittle
> per-branch ordering alone), read `feature_` before running callbacks,
> and resolve `callback_` on empty input or session/client disconnect.
>
> Fixed: 570347667, 562796602
> Test: components_unittests --gtest_filter=SessionImplTest.SetInput*
